0_(1F) Puffballs, earthstars, and bird's nest fungi – these basidiomycetes are distinctive fungi that typically are easy to identify to the broad group. Puffballs and earthstars are closely related in the order Lycoperdales; bird's nest fungi are in the order Nidulariales. 010182241132280Puffballs, earthstars, and bird's nest fungi0
0a _(1F) Puffballs010182251132290102
0b _(1F) Earthstars010182261132300123
0c _(1F) Bird's nest fungi010182271132310127
0_(87a) 01022252281142320Puffballs – rounded fruiting bodies that become dry at maturity, releasing spores through cracks or a hole _(ostiole) that develops as the puffball grows. With or without a stalk to support the fruiting bodyPuffballs0
0a _(87a) Round to pear shaped, powdery surface at maturity; without a stalk _(true puffballs)01022252291142330103
0b _(87a) Round to pear shaped on a distinctive stalk _(stalked puffballs)01022252301142340115
0c _(87a) Resembling a puffball or an immature mushroom that never opens; may be brittle or tough at maturity but never powdery _(false puffballs)01022252311142350120
0_(102a) True puffballs Lycoperdales, Basidiomycetes. These do not have a stem, and usually are round to pear-shaped. The outer peridium does not recurve to form rays like an earthstar. All true puffballs have powdery glebas _(spore masses) at maturity, which range from yellow to black. 01032292321152360True puffballs0
0a _(102a) Young puffball cut in half has firm dark purplish spore mass _(gleba); skin is often thick01032292331152370104
0b _(102a) Young puffball cut in half has firm white spore mass _(gleba); skin is usually thin01032292341152380107
0a _(103a) Fruit body 3-6 cm across, outer skin splitting into lobes but never curving back01042332351162390105
0b _(103a) Fruit body 4-14 cm across, outer skin splitting and curving back like an earthstar01042332361162400106
0a _(104a) Outer skin covered with warts 01052352371172410Scleroderma aurantium0
0b _(104a) Outer skin smooth 01052352381172420Scleroderma bovista0
0a _(104b) Outer skin cracked and roughened 01062362391182430Scleroderma geaster0
0b _(104b) Outer skin smooth 01062362401182440Scleroderma flavidum0
0a _(103b) Round, oval or flattened oval; >10 cm across; if pear shaped then > 8cm across01072342411192450108
0b _(103b) Round, < 6cm across01072342421192460109
0c _(103b) Pear shaped or nearly so, with a sterile base; < 7cm across01072342431192470113
0a _(107a) Puffball 10-20 cm across; surface cracked to form irregular scales 01082412441202480Calvatia lepidophora0
0b _(107a) Puffball 20-50 cm across; surface very smooth 01082412451202490Calvatia gigantea0
0c _(107a) Puffball 20-50 cm across; surface sculptured and cracked 01082412461202500Calvatia booniana0
0d _(107a) Puffball 8-15 cm across; outer skin with pyramid-shaped warts 01082412471202510Calvatia sculpta0
