0_(102b) Stalked Puffballs Tulostomatales. This group is united by having a stalk which can be dry, gelatinous, or woody. Most are mycorrhizal. 01152302631272670Stalked Puffballs Tulostomatales0
0a _(102b) Club shaped fruit body, stalk not separated from spore sac, gleba with numerous chambers 01152302641272680Pisolithus tinctorius0
0b _(102b) Spherical to oval spore sac on a cylindrical stalk; gleba powdery and homogeneous01152302651272690116
0a _(115b) Stalk covered with a thick gelatinous layer that may have chambers01162652661282700117
0b _(115b) Stalk thick or woody but never gelatinous01162652671282710118
0a _(116a) Spore sac red, at first covered with a thick red gelatinous layer _(common name is apt: the slimy stalked puffball) 01172662681292720Calostoma cinnabaria0
