0_(1H) Coral fungi are basidiomycetes and their fruiting bodies are finger or club shaped, erect, typically brittle or tough, and can be large and brightly coloured. Fruit bodies can be single or branched, and the branches can be cylindrical or flattened A398-414; M232-40 01474123561593600Coral fungi0
