0_(1I) Jelly fungi are heterobasidiomycetes in the order Tremellales. Fruiting bodies typically are small and brightly coloured, usually on wood. Their gelatinous flesh becomes tough and may be inconspicuous in dry weather. A379-86; M317-23 0154113751663790Jelly fungi0
