0_(1J) Stinkhorns, basidiomycete order Phallales. These are distinctive fungi whose spore masses are borne in pits or on the tip of a 2-10cm tall stem in a smelly slime that is attractive to flies. Stinkhorns develop within an egg-like structure until the spores are fully mature, like the related groups puffballs and earth stars. 01594093881713920Stinkhorns0
0a _(1J) Spore slime exposed or borne aloft at maturity; fruiting body variously shaped, emergiung from an “egg” whose skin _(peridium) forms a sack at the base01594093891713930160
